(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[8 1 "// The module _ast (PY6a; Python/Python-ast.c): AST and its node classes, made at the module's first import"] [9 1 "// from astTable (Parser/Python.asdl, tools/pyi/asdl_table.py) as heap classes of the module \"ast\", each with"] [10 1 "// _fields, _attributes and __match_args__; AST's __init__ takes the fields by position and keyword (a missing"] [11 1 "// sequence field []; an optional field or attribute None at class level), __repr__ is 3.14's. compile()'s"] [12 1 "// PyCF_ONLY_AST, the forms-to-ast bridge, is the next step (ast.parse raises naming it)."] [14 1 "// astQuals are each node class's fields and attributes with their quantifiers (\"\", \"?\", \"*\")."] [45 1 "// astQualsOf is the node class's fields' and attributes' quantifiers, from its MRO's first table class."] [55 1 "// astInit is ast_type_init (3.14's rules): the fields by position and keyword; a keyword neither a field nor an"] [56 1 "// attribute a DeprecationWarning; a field not given, by its _field_types entry: an optional one left to the class's"] [57 1 "// None, a list one [], an expr_context Load(), else a DeprecationWarning (missing from _field_types, or required)."] [66 1 "// astInitKeys is astInit with the keywords' keys as the kwargs dict holds them (queue 250): a key that is no str"] [67 1 "// reaches it from a ** call (kwDictCall), compared with the fields by ==, warned of, and refused by setattr."] [179 3 "// a user's subclass without _field_types: the fields not given do not exist, as before 3.13"] [195 4 "// optional: the class's None"] [223 1 "// astInitB is AST's __init__ (kwDictCall: a node class whose __init__ is still AST's)."] [226 1 "// kwDictCall is a call f(*args, **kw) whose kw has a key that is no str (queue 250), for the callables whose C"] [227 1 "// implementation takes the kwargs dict itself in CPython rather than through vectorcall's keyword names"] [228 1 "// (_PyStack_UnpackDict's \"keywords must be strings\"): a node class's construction (type_call's tp_init,"] [229 1 "// ast_type_init) and a node's __replace__ (ast_type_replace). handled false for any other callable."] [279 3 "// ast_type_replace's PySet_Discard(expecting, key) in the dict's order: a key that is not expected refused"] [287 5 "// a key equal to an expected name (its own __eq__ and __hash__) is not refused here: left to the"] [288 5 "// TypeError of the call's keyword names"] [307 1 "// astTpName is the class's tp_name in CPython's messages: \"ast.AST\" for AST (a static type's spec name), the name of"] [308 1 "// the node classes and of the user's classes (heap types)."] [316 1 "// astExprContext and astLoad are the classes expr_context and Load (ast_type_init's expr_context default)."] [319 1 "// astGetItemOptional is o[key], nil when the key is missing (PyDict_GetItemWithError on a dict, else a KeyError caught)."] [334 1 "// astReplace is ast_type_replace (copy.replace): the node's fields and attributes, then the keywords, given to its"] [335 1 "// class; a keyword neither a field nor an attribute, or a required field neither on the node nor given, a TypeError."] [445 1 "// astReduce is ast_type_reduce: (class, a None per field the node has up to the first it lacks, __dict__)."] [480 1 "// astRepr is ast_repr_max_depth (3.14): Name(...) past the depth, Name() without fields, else each field's"] [481 1 "// value, a list's or tuple's by astReprList, a node's one level deeper."] [527 1 "// astReprList is ast_repr_list: [] as repr, else the first and the last item (\"...\" between when more), a node one"] [528 1 "// level deeper."] [576 1 "// astSignature is a constructor's or product's __doc__ (asdl_c.py): NAME(TYPE[?*] FIELD, ...), NAME without fields;"] [577 1 "// Python.asdl's two \"expr?*\" sequences (Dict's keys, arguments' kw_defaults) as written there."] [626 2 "// AST's methods bind to the instance as method descriptors (methodDescrs; queue 202c: super().__init__ of a node"] [627 2 "// class's subclass, node.__replace__)"] [645 24 "// each node class's fields, for _field_types once every class exists"] [662 28 "// an optional attribute's default, at class level as CPython's"] [702 27 "// an optional field's default, at class level"] [723 2 "// a sum's __doc__ (asdl_c.py's visitSum): \"name = C1 | C2\" for a simple one, else one constructor a line"] [731 2 "// _field_types (CPython's add_ast_annotations: ast.dump reads it): a field's type, list[T] for a sequence, T | None"] [732 2 "// for an optional one (PY6h's REQUEST, queue 200)"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[48 26] [104 32] [107 26] [139 37] [148 27] [158 128] [167 41] [191 79] [201 41] [210 36] [215 79] [248 47] [274 25] [290 36] [321 23] [365 24] [386 24] [395 50] [397 33] [399 24] [433 37] [509 31] [515 23] [542 30] [745 26]]} (go/file "builtins_ast.go" :imports [


